{"id":"mahabharata-3-164","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":164,"title":"चतुःषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 164 · Arjuna in Indra's heaven","summary":{"en":"Arjuna tells how the world-guardians gave him their weapons, how Matali carried him to Indra's heaven, and how he lived there five years learning divine weapons and music. Indra then asked as his teacher's fee that he destroy the Nivatakavacas.","kn":"ಲೋಕಪಾಲರು ತಮ್ಮ ಅಸ್ತ್ರಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಟ್ಟದ್ದು, ಮಾತಲಿ ತನ್ನನ್ನು ಇಂದ್ರಲೋಕಕ್ಕೆ ಒಯ್ದದ್ದು, ಅಲ್ಲಿ ಐದು ವರ್ಷ ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರ ಸಂಗೀತಗಳನ್ನು ಕಲಿತದ್ದು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅನಂತರ ಗುರುದಕ್ಷಿಣೆಯಾಗಿ ನಿವಾತಕವಚರನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡೆಂದು ಇಂದ್ರನು ಕೇಳಿದನು.","hi":"अर्जुन बताते हैं कि लोकपालों ने उन्हें अपने अस्त्र दिए, मातलि उन्हें इन्द्रलोक ले गए, और वहाँ वे पाँच वर्ष दिव्यास्त्र और संगीत सीखते रहे। तब इन्द्र ने गुरुदक्षिणा में निवातकवचों के विनाश की माँग की।","te":"లోకపాలకులు తమ అస్త్రాలను ఇవ్వడం, మాతలి తనను ఇంద్రలోకానికి తీసుకువెళ్లడం, అక్కడ ఐదేళ్లు దివ్యాస్త్రాలు, సంగీతం నేర్చుకోవడం అర్జునుడు చెబుతాడు. తర్వాత గురుదక్షిణగా నివాతకవచులను నాశనం చేయమని ఇంద్రుడు అడిగాడు.","ta":"லோகபாலர்கள் தங்கள் அஸ்திரங்களைக் கொடுத்ததையும், மாதலி தன்னை இந்திரலோகத்துக்கு அழைத்துச் சென்றதையும், அங்கு ஐந்து ஆண்டுகள் தெய்வீக அஸ்திரங்களும் இசையும் கற்றதையும் அர்ஜுனன் சொல்கிறான். பின்னர் குருதக்ஷிணையாக நிவாதகவசர்களை அழிக்குமாறு இந்திரன் கேட்டான்.","ml":"ലോകപാലകന്മാർ തങ്ങളുടെ ആയുധങ്ങൾ നൽകിയതും, മാതലി തന്നെ ഇന്ദ്രലോകത്തേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോയതും, അവിടെ അഞ്ചു വർഷം ദിവ്യായുധങ്ങളും സംഗീതവും പഠിച്ച് കഴിഞ്ഞതും അർജുനൻ പറയുന്നു. പിന്നെ ഗുരുദക്ഷിണയായി നിവാതകവചന്മാരെ നശിപ്പിക്കാൻ ഇന്ദ്രൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെട്ടതും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.164; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्तामवसं प्रीतो रजनीं तत्र भारत ।\nप्रसादाद्देवदेवस्य त्र्यम्बकस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then, Bharata, I spent that night there, glad, by the grace of the great-souled three-eyed god of gods.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"व्युषितो रजनीं चाहं कृत्वा पूर्वाह्णिकक्रियाम् ।\nअपश्यं तं द्विजश्रेष्ठं दृष्टवानस्मि यं पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having passed the night and done my morning rites, I saw that best of brahmins whom I had seen before.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"तस्मै चाहं यथावृत्तं सर्वमेव न्यवेदयम् ।\nभगवन्तं महादेवं समेतोऽस्मीति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I told him everything as it happened, that I had met the blessed Mahadeva, Bharata.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"स मामुवाच राजेन्द्र प्रीयमाणो द्विजोत्तमः ।\nदृष्टस्त्वया महादेवो यथा नान्येन केनचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He, the best of brahmins, said to me gladly, king: 'You have seen Mahadeva as no one else has.'\""}},{"n":5,"text":"समेत्य लोकपालैस्तु सर्वैर्वैवस्वतादिभिः ।\nद्रष्टास्यनघ देवेन्द्रं स च तेऽस्त्राणि दास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Having met all the guardians of the world, Vaivasvata and the others, you will, blameless one, see the king of gods, and he will give you weapons.'\""}},{"n":6,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा स मां राजन्नाश्लिष्य च पुनः पुनः ।\nअगच्छत्स यथाकामं ब्राह्मणः सूर्यसंनिभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having said this, king, and embraced me again and again, the brahmin, bright as the sun, went where he wished.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"अथापराह्णे तस्याह्नः प्रावात्पुण्यः समीरणः ।\nपुनर्नवमिमं लोकं कुर्वन्निव सपत्नहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then in the afternoon of that day a holy breeze blew, as if making this world new again, slayer of rivals.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"दिव्यानि चैव माल्यानि सुगन्धीनि नवानि च ।\nशैशिरस्य गिरेः पादे प्रादुरासन्समीपतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Divine garlands, fragrant and fresh, appeared near the foot of the snowy mountain.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"वादित्राणि च दिव्यानि सुघोषाणि समन्ततः ।\nस्तुतयश्चेन्द्रसंयुक्ता अश्रूयन्त मनोहराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"On every side divine instruments sounded sweetly, and charming hymns in praise of Indra were heard.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"गणाश्चाप्सरसां तत्र गन्धर्वाणां तथैव च ।\nपुरस्ताद्देवदेवस्य जगुर्गीतानि सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Troops of Apsarases and Gandharvas sang songs everywhere before the god of gods.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"मरुतां च गणास्तत्र देवयानैरुपागमन् ।\nमहेन्द्रानुचरा ये च देवसद्मनिवासिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Troops of the Maruts came there in divine vehicles, with Mahendra's attendants and those living in the abodes of the gods.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो मरुत्वान्हरिभिर्युक्तैर्वाहैः स्वलंकृतैः ।\nशचीसहायस्तत्रायात्सह सर्वैस्तदामरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then Marutvan, Indra, came with his well-adorned bay horses and Shachi beside him, with all the immortals.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु कुबेरो नरवाहनः ।\nदर्शयामास मां राजँल्लक्ष्म्या परमया युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Just then Kubera, whose vehicle is men, showed himself to me, king, in supreme splendour.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"दक्षिणस्यां दिशि यमं प्रत्यपश्यं व्यवस्थितम् ।\nवरुणं देवराजं च यथास्थानमवस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the southern quarter I saw Yama standing, and Varuna and the king of the gods, each in his place.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"ते मामूचुर्महाराज सान्त्वयित्वा सुरर्षभाः ।\nसव्यसाचिन्समीक्षस्व लोकपालानवस्थितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They comforted me, great king, and said, 'Savyasachin, look at the guardians of the world standing here.'\""}},{"n":16,"text":"सुरकार्यार्थसिद्ध्यर्थं दृष्टवानसि शंकरम् ।\nअस्मत्तोऽपि गृहाण त्वमस्त्राणीति समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You have seen Shankara for the accomplishment of the gods' work. Take weapons from us too, from every side.'\""}},{"n":17,"text":"ततोऽहं प्रयतो भूत्वा प्रणिपत्य सुरर्षभान् ।\nप्रत्यगृह्णं तदास्त्राणि महान्ति विधिवत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then, with discipline, I bowed to the best of the gods and duly accepted the great weapons, lord.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"गृहीतास्त्रस्ततो देवैरनुज्ञातोऽस्मि भारत ।\nअथ देवा ययुः सर्वे यथागतमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When I had received the weapons, Bharata, the gods gave me leave, and then all the gods went away as they came, tamer of foes.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"मघवानपि देवेशो रथमारुह्य सुप्रभम् ।\nउवाच भगवान्वाक्यं स्मयन्निव सुरारिहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Maghavan too, the lord of gods, mounting his bright chariot, said, the blessed destroyer of the gods' foes seeming to smile,\""}},{"n":20,"text":"पुरैवागमनादस्माद्वेदाहं त्वां धनंजय ।\nअतः परं त्वहं वै त्वां दर्शये भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'I have known you, Dhananjaya, since before this coming. Now I show myself to you, bull of the Bharatas.'\""}},{"n":21,"text":"त्वया हि तीर्थेषु पुरा समाप्लावः कृतोऽसकृत् ।\nतपश्चेदं पुरा तप्तं स्वर्गं गन्तासि पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You bathed often in holy places before and practised this austerity; you will go to heaven, Pandava.'\""}},{"n":22,"text":"भूयश्चैव तु तप्तव्यं तपः परमदारुणम् ।\nउवाच भगवान्सर्वं तपसश्चोपपादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You must again practise very severe austerity.' The blessed one told me everything about preparing for that austerity.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"मातलिर्मन्नियोगात्त्वां त्रिदिवं प्रापयिष्यति ।\nविदितस्त्वं हि देवानामृषीणां च महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'By my command Matali will take you to heaven. You are known to the gods and great-souled sages.'\""}},{"n":24,"text":"ततोऽहमब्रुवं शक्रं प्रसीद भगवन्मम ।\nआचार्यं वरये त्वाहमस्त्रार्थं त्रिदशेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I said to Shakra, 'Be gracious to me, lord. I choose you as teacher for the sake of weapons, lord of the thirty gods.'\""}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"क्रूरं कर्मास्त्रवित्तात करिष्यसि परंतप ।\nयदर्थमस्त्राणीप्सुस्त्वं तं कामं पाण्डवाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dear one, tamer of foes, you who know weapons will do a cruel act. Pandava, gain the wish for which you seek weapons.\""}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"ततोऽहमब्रुवं नाहं दिव्यान्यस्त्राणि शत्रुहन् ।\nमानुषेषु प्रयोक्ष्यामि विनास्त्रप्रतिघातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I said, 'Slayer of foes, I will not use the divine weapons against humans, except to counter weapons.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तानि दिव्यानि मेऽस्त्राणि प्रयच्छ विबुधाधिप ।\nलोकांश्चास्त्रजितान्पश्चाल्लभेयं सुरपुंगव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Give me those divine weapons, lord of the gods, so that afterwards I may win the worlds won by weapons, bull of the gods.'\""}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"परीक्षार्थं मयैतत्ते वाक्यमुक्तं धनंजय ।\nममात्मजस्य वचनं सूपपन्नमिदं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I said this to you as a test, Dhananjaya. This reply of yours, as my son, is very fitting.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"शिक्ष मे भवनं गत्वा सर्वाण्यस्त्राणि भारत ।\nवायोरग्नेर्वसुभ्योऽथ वरुणात्समरुद्गणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Come to my abode and learn all the weapons, Bharata, from Vayu, Agni, the Vasus, Varuna and the Maruts.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"साध्यं पैतामहं चैव गन्धर्वोरगरक्षसाम् ।\nवैष्णवानि च सर्वाणि नैरृतानि तथैव च ।\nमद्गतानि च यानीह सर्वास्त्राणि कुरूद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Sadhya weapon, and that of the Grandfather, those of Gandharvas, serpents and rakshasas, all those of Vishnu, and those of Nirriti, and all the weapons that are with me here, bearer of the Kuru line.\""}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु मां शक्रस्तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ।\nअथापश्यं हरियुजं रथमैन्द्रमुपस्थितम् ।\nदिव्यं मायामयं पुण्यं यत्तं मातलिना नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having said this, Shakra vanished on the spot. Then I saw Indra's chariot, yoked with bay horses, divine, full of magic and holy, held by Matali, king.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"लोकपालेषु यातेषु मामुवाचाथ मातलिः ।\nद्रष्टुमिच्छति शक्रस्त्वां देवराजो महाद्युते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When the guardians of the world had gone, Matali said to me, 'Shakra, the king of the gods, wishes to see you, radiant one.'\""}},{"n":33,"text":"संसिद्धस्त्वं महाबाहो कुरु कार्यमनुत्तमम् ।\nपश्य पुण्यकृतां लोकान्सशरीरो दिवं व्रज ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'You are perfected, mighty-armed one; do the unsurpassed task. See the worlds of the virtuous, and go to heaven in your body.'\""}},{"n":34,"text":"इत्युक्तोऽहं मातलिना गिरिमामन्त्र्य शैशिरम् ।\nप्रदक्षिणमुपावृत्य समारोहं रथोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Told this by Matali, I took leave of the snowy mountain, circled it to the right and mounted the best of chariots.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"चोदयामास स हयान्मनोमारुतरंहसः ।\nमातलिर्हयशास्त्रज्ञो यथावद्भूरिदक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Matali, who knew the science of horses and was generous in gifts, urged on the horses, swift as mind and wind.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"अवैक्षत च मे वक्त्रं स्थितस्याथ स सारथिः ।\nतथा भ्रान्ते रथे राजन्विस्मितश्चेदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As I stood, the charioteer watched my face, and when the chariot whirled, king, he said in wonder:\""}},{"n":37,"text":"अत्यद्भुतमिदं मेऽद्य विचित्रं प्रतिभाति माम् ।\nयदास्थितो रथं दिव्यं पदा न चलितो भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'This seems to me today very wonderful and strange, that you, standing in the divine chariot, were not moved from your footing.'\""}},{"n":38,"text":"देवराजोऽपि हि मया नित्यमत्रोपलक्षितः ।\nविचलन्प्रथमोत्पाते हयानां भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Even the king of the gods, bull of the Bharatas, I have always seen shake at the first lurch of the horses.'\""}},{"n":39,"text":"त्वं पुनः स्थित एवात्र रथे भ्रान्ते कुरूद्वह ।\nअतिशक्रमिदं सत्त्वं तवेति प्रतिभाति मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'But you stood firm on the chariot as it whirled, bearer of the Kuru line. This strength of yours seems to me beyond Shakra's.'\""}},{"n":40,"text":"इत्युक्त्वाकाशमाविश्य मातलिर्विबुधालयान् ।\nदर्शयामास मे राजन्विमानानि च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having said this, Matali entered the sky and showed me the abodes of the gods and their celestial cars, king.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"नन्दनादीनि देवानां वनानि बहुलान्युत ।\nदर्शयामास मे प्रीत्या मातलिः शक्रसारथिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Matali, Shakra's charioteer, lovingly showed me Nandana and the many other woods of the gods.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"ततः शक्रस्य भवनमपश्यममरावतीम् ।\nदिव्यैः कामफलैर्वृक्षै रत्नैश्च समलंकृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I saw Shakra's home, Amaravati, adorned with divine wish-granting trees and jewels.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"न तां भासयते सूर्यो न शीतोष्णे न च क्लमः ।\nरजः पङ्को न च तमस्तत्रास्ति न जरा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The sun does not light it; there is no cold or heat, no weariness, no dust or mud, no darkness and no old age, king.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"न तत्र शोको दैन्यं वा वैवर्ण्यं चोपलक्ष्यते ।\nदिवौकसां महाराज न च ग्लानिररिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"No grief, wretchedness or discolouring is seen there among the dwellers in heaven, great king, and no weariness, tamer of foes.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"न क्रोधलोभौ तत्रास्तामशुभं च विशां पते ।\nनित्यतुष्टाश्च हृष्टाश्च प्राणिनः सुरवेश्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There were no anger or greed there, nor anything inauspicious, lord of the people. The beings in the home of the gods are always contented and glad.\""}},{"n":46,"text":"नित्यपुष्पफलास्तत्र पादपा हरितच्छदाः ।\nपुष्करिण्यश्च विविधाः पद्मसौगन्धिकायुताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The trees there bear flowers and fruit always and have green leaves, and there are many ponds with lotuses and saugandhikas.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"शीतस्तत्र ववौ वायुः सुगन्धो जीवनः शुचिः ।\nसर्वरत्नविचित्रा च भूमिः पुष्पविभूषिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A cool, fragrant, life-giving, pure wind blew there, and the ground, rich in every jewel, was adorned with flowers.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"मृगद्विजाश्च बहवो रुचिरा मधुरस्वराः ।\nविमानयायिनश्चात्र दृश्यन्ते बहवोऽमराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Many lovely, sweet-voiced beasts and birds, and many immortals travelling in aerial cars, were seen there.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"ततोऽपश्यं वसून्रुद्रान्साध्यांश्च समरुद्गणान् ।\nआदित्यानश्विनौ चैव तान्सर्वान्प्रत्यपूजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I saw the Vasus, Rudras, Sadhyas with the Maruts, the Adityas and the two Ashvins, and I honoured them all in return.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"ते मां वीर्येण यशसा तेजसा च बलेन च ।\nअस्त्रैश्चाप्यन्वजानन्त संग्रामविजयेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They welcomed me for my valour, fame, splendour, strength, weapons and victory in battle.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"प्रविश्य तां पुरीं रम्यां देवगन्धर्वसेविताम् ।\nदेवराजं सहस्राक्षमुपातिष्ठं कृताञ्जलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Entering that lovely city, served by gods and Gandharvas, I stood with folded hands before the thousand-eyed king of the gods.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"ददावर्धासनं प्रीतः शक्रो मे ददतां वरः ।\nबहुमानाच्च गात्राणि पस्पर्श मम वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Pleased, Shakra, best of givers, gave me half his seat, and Vasava touched my limbs with great regard.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"तत्राहं देवगन्धर्वैः सहितो भूरिदक्षिण ।\nअस्त्रार्थमवसं स्वर्गे कुर्वाणोऽस्त्राणि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There, generous king, I lived in heaven with the gods and Gandharvas, working at the weapons for the sake of weapons, Bharata.\""}},{"n":54,"text":"विश्वावसोश्च मे पुत्रश्चित्रसेनोऽभवत्सखा ।\nस च गान्धर्वमखिलं ग्राहयामास मां नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Chitrasena, son of Vishvavasu, became my friend, and he had me learn all of Gandharva lore, king.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"ततोऽहमवसं राजन्गृहीतास्त्रः सुपूजितः ।\nसुखं शक्रस्य भवने सर्वकामसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then, king, I lived there, my weapons taken, much honoured, in comfort in Shakra's abode, supplied with every desire.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"शृण्वन्वै गीतशब्दं च तूर्यशब्दं च पुष्कलम् ।\nपश्यंश्चाप्सरसः श्रेष्ठा नृत्यमानाः परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing singing and abundant music, and seeing the finest Apsarases dancing, tamer of foes,\""}},{"n":57,"text":"तत्सर्वमनवज्ञाय तथ्यं विज्ज्ञाय भारत ।\nअत्यर्थं प्रतिगृह्याहमस्त्रेष्वेव व्यवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I paid no heed to any of it, knowing what was true, Bharata, and, receiving much, I stayed fixed on the weapons alone.\""}},{"n":58,"text":"ततोऽतुष्यत्सहस्राक्षस्तेन कामेन मे विभुः ।\nएवं मे वसतो राजन्नेष कालोऽत्यगाद्दिवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then the thousand-eyed lord was pleased with that wish of mine. So, king, while I lived thus, this time passed in heaven.\""}}]}]}